# The platform passes these to each process when it starts the app. Nothing
# reads this file; it only documents the names, for running the app elsewhere.
#
# client (npm run dev in client/)
#   PORT               the port the Vite dev server listens on
#   ICOD_PORT_API      the server's port, which /api is forwarded to
#   ICOD_PREVIEW_HOST  the public preview host name, if any
#
# server (npm run dev in server/)
#   PORT               the port the API listens on
#   DATABASE_URL       the MongoDB connection string
#
# The user's own variables are in .env beside this file (and .env.production for
# the deployed app), set under Environment Variables and never committed. The
# server loads .env when it starts (--env-file-if-exists=../.env), the client
# through Vite's envDir; a variable the platform passes always wins.
